+// character-density guess whose bias against a real tokenizer is large and
+// content-dependent (measured ~1.2-1.5x low on tool output such as log text),
+// so re-estimating the WHOLE conversation on every request compounds that bias
+// across the entire history. Instead, remember the provider's own reported
+// prompt-token count for the previous request of this session and estimate only
+// the DELTA appended since then: the bulk of the request is then exact, and only
+// the newly appended content (usually one tool result) carries heuristic error.
